{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מזי רעב", :translit "meizei ra'av", :gloss "terrors of hunger"} {:he "מזי רעב. ולחומי רשף. וקטב מרירי. ושן בהמות. עם חמת זוחלי עפר", :translit "meizei ra'av, v'lahumei reshef, v'ketav meriri, v'shen behemot, im chamat zochlei afar", :gloss "terrors of hunger, and flames of lightning, and bitter destruction, and teeth of beasts, with the venom of crawlers of dust"} {:he "חומשי תורה", :translit "chumshei torah", :gloss "fifths of the Torah"} {:he "ה' ניאופים, בהושע", :translit "hamishah ni'ufim, be'hoshea", :gloss "five acts of adultery, in Hosea"} {:he "ה' תועבות שראה יחזקאל", :translit "hamishah to'evot she'ra'ah y'chezkel", :gloss "five abominations that Ezekiel saw"} {:he "המקטירי'. לבעל. לשמש. ולירח. ולמזלות. ולכל צבא השמים", :translit "hamaq'tirim. la'ba'al. la'shamesh. v'la'yare'ach. v'la'mazalot. v'le'chol tzeva ha'shamayim", :gloss "those who offer incense: to Baal, to the sun, and to the moon, and to the constellations, and to all the host of the heavens"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Structural correspondence: five destructive forces listed in the verse mirror five categories of Israel's transgressions against God."}], :frame {:text "The verse (Deuteronomy 32:24) enumerates five agents of destruction: מזי רעב, ולחומי רשף, וקטב מרירי, ושן בהמות, עם חמת זוחלי עפר. Hosea 2:4–2:6 rebukes Israel with a recurring accusation of adultery, and Hosea 2:9–2:12 condemns Baal worship. Ezekiel 8 records five abominations the prophet is shown: the idol of jealousy (Ezekiel 8:5), the seventy elders offering incense (Ezekiel 8:10–11), women weeping for Tammuz (Ezekiel 8:14), and men worshipping the sun (Ezekiel 8:16). Zephaniah 1:5 condemns those who worship the host of heaven. The Ba'al HaTurim compresses these strands into a single typological reading in which five punishments correspond to five categories of sin.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 32:24" "Hosea 2:4" "Hosea 2:9" "Ezekiel 8:5" "Ezekiel 8:10" "Ezekiel 8:14" "Ezekiel 8:16" "Zephaniah 1:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Structural correspondence: five destructive forces listed in the verse mirror five categories of Israel's transgressions against God.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:41:04.468068417Z", :model "glm-5.2"}